maso d'Aquino","target":"San Tommaso d'Aquino","line":14},{"title":"Tomismo","target":"Tomismo","line":15},{"title":"god-philosophy-universities","target":"god-philosophy-universities","line":16},{"title":"le-thomisme-gilson","target":"le-thomisme-gilson","line":31},{"title":"le-thomisme-gilson","target":"le-thomisme-gilson","line":33},{"title":"god-philosophy-universities","target":"god-philosophy-universities","line":60}],"metadata":{"type":"source","title":"De regimine principum ad regem Cypri (\"Principi non negoziabili sulla società e sulla politica\")","address":"c-000035","created":"2026-07-25","updated":"2026-07-25","tags":["#tomismo","#source","#primary-text","#political-philosophy"],"status":"developing","related":["[[San Tommaso d'Aquino]]","[[Tomismo]]","[[god-philosophy-universities]]"],"source_type":"book","author":"San Tommaso d'Aquino (Libro I, Libro II capp. 1-4); continuato da Tolomeo da Lucca (rest.)","date_published":"1265-1266 (Aquinas's authentic portion, per Mandonnet); continuation by Ptolemy of Lucca after 1274","url":"","confidence":"high","key_claims":["Monarchy (rule by one) is the best form of government because unity of the ruler best secures the common good of peace, mirroring how nature always governs through a single principle (the heart in the body, reason in the soul, one God ruling the universe).","By the same logic of unity, tyranny (corrupt one-man rule) is the worst regime — worse than oligarchy, worse than democracy — because a unified evil is more effective/destructive than a divided one; tyrants specifically suppress solidarity, virtue, and trust among subjects to prevent organized resistance.","Historical case studies (Rome's shift from kings to consuls to emperors; the Hebrew people's judges-then-kings history) illustrate the real danger on both sides: fear of tyranny driving people to reject good kingship, versus the risk that legitimate kingship degenerates into tyranny."],"raw_file":".raw/S. Tommaso d'Aquino - Principi non Negoziabili sulla Società e sulla Politica.epub"},"task_lines":[],"tasks":{},"codeblock_ranges":[]},"smart_blocks:Wiki/sources/principi-non-negoziabili-de-regimine.md#---frontmatter---": {"path":null,"last_embed":{"hash":null},"embeddings":{},"text":null,"length":0,"last_read":{"hash":"8jipau","at":1785014026854},"key":"Wiki/sources/principi-non-negoziabili-de-regimine.md#---frontmatter---","lines":[1,27],"size":1613,"outlinks":[{"title":"San Tommaso d'Aquino","target":"San Tommaso d'Aquino","line":14},{"title":"Tomismo","target":"Tomismo","line":15},{"title":"god-philosophy-universities","target":"god-philosophy-universities","line":16}],"class_name":"SmartBlock"},
